{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS27xQV3y38W73W7bDqz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018GdVHhTxbFsZYUjVwj3uNJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-42i1JB; python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('status=$?','rc=$?').replace('$status','$rc')\ns=s.replace('claude -p','# Headless runs have no login session; needs CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (from `claude setup-token`).\\nclaude -p',1)\ns=s.replace('''\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"''','''\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\" \\\\\n  || echo \"notify failed\" >&2''')\ns=s.replace('''  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\"''','''  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\" || echo \"notify failed\" >&2''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='bin/notify.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('curl -sS -X','curl -sS -f -X')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review never reports anything\n\n1. **The job itself can't run `claude`: \"Not logged in · Please run /login\"** (every run in `nightly-review.err`).\n   The launchd agent has no access to the interactive login session, so headless `claude -p` has no credentials.\n   Fix (needs you, I can't do it here): run `claude setup-token` once and give the job the token, e.g.\n   `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the plist's `EnvironmentVariables` (or read it from the keychain in the script),\n   then `launchctl bootout` / `bootstrap` the agent again.\n\n2. **The failure handler crashes before it can notify.** `status=$?` in zsh assigns to the read-only special\n   variable `status`, which aborts the script (`read-only variable: status`, line 19, exit 1). So the\n   \"FAILED\" Telegram message was never sent. Fixed by renaming the variable to `rc`.\n\n3. **Notifier hardening (secondary).** `notify.sh` used `curl -sS` with output discarded, so Telegram HTTP errors\n   (bad token/chat) exited 0 silently. Added `-f`. The scripts now log \"notify failed\" to stderr if notifying fails.\n   Also note `security find-generic-password` can fail from launchd if the keychain is locked;\n   if the err log shows that after fixing 1–2, set `TG_BOT_TOKEN` in the plist environment instead.\n\nNot a cause: schedule and paths are fine (`runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1` in launchctl-print.txt); PATH is OK as `claude` was found.\nE\ngit diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2737,"cache_read_input_tokens":20613,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2737},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c92a228c-0aac-43ea-a625-afd5e003d6d2","uuid":"bd2341eb-dbd9-4ec1-a24e-a68d69c4fe5f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:19:37.244Z","request_id":"req_011CgS27x8c1acJNdVrvjpLA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018GdVHhTxbFsZYUjVwj3uNJ":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-42i1JB; python3 - <<'E'\np='bin/nightly-review.zsh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('status=$?','rc=$?').replace('$status','$rc')\ns=s.replace('claude -p','# Headless runs have no login session; needs CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (from `claude setup-token`).\\nclaude -p',1)\ns=s.replace('''\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"''','''\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\" \\\\\n  || echo \"notify failed\" >&2''')\ns=s.replace('''  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\"''','''  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\" || echo \"notify failed\" >&2''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='bin/notify.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('curl -sS -X','curl -sS -f -X')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why nightly-review never reports anything\n\n1. **The job itself can't run `claude`: \"Not logged in · Please run /login\"** (every run in `nightly-review.err`).\n   The launchd agent has no access to the interactive login session, so headless `claude -p` has no credentials.\n   Fix (needs you, I can't do it here): run `claude setup-token` once and give the job the token, e.g.\n   `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` in the plist's `EnvironmentVariables` (or read it from the keychain in the script),\n   then `launchctl bootout` / `bootstrap` the agent again.\n\n2. **The failure handler crashes before it can notify.** `status=$?` in zsh assigns to the read-only special\n   variable `status`, which aborts the script (`read-only variable: status`, line 19, exit 1). So the\n   \"FAILED\" Telegram message was never sent. Fixed by renaming the variable to `rc`.\n\n3. **Notifier hardening (secondary).** `notify.sh` used `curl -sS` with output discarded, so Telegram HTTP errors\n   (bad token/chat) exited 0 silently. Added `-f`. The scripts now log \"notify failed\" to stderr if notifying fails.\n   Also note `security find-generic-password` can fail from launchd if the keychain is locked;\n   if the err log shows that after fixing 1–2, set `TG_BOT_TOKEN` in the plist environment instead.\n\nNot a cause: schedule and paths are fine (`runs = 6`, `last exit code = 1` in launchctl-print.txt); PATH is OK as `claude` was found.\nE\ngit diff --stat"}}}
