{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS28rfymt8kxDfx9ZyP8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has run six times and failed every time. Two things stopped any report from reaching you: `claude` isn't logged in under launchd, and the failure handler in the script crashes before it can send anything. I couldn't run the job or the notifier here, so none of this was tested. I read it from the logs and `launchctl-print.txt`.\n\n1. **`claude` isn't logged in under launchd.** Every run in `nightly-review.err` logs \"Not logged in · Please run /login\". The launchd agent can't use your interactive login, so `claude -p` has no credentials. I can't fix this one from here. Run `claude setup-token` once. Then put the token in the plist's `EnvironmentVariables` as `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, or have the script read it from the keychain. Then reload the agent with `launchctl bootout` and `bootstrap`. I only added a comment about this in the script.\n2. **The failure handler crashes.** `status=$?` in zsh assigns to a read-only special variable, so the script aborts with \"read-only variable: status\" at line 19. The \"FAILED\" Telegram message was never sent. I renamed the variable to `rc` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh`.\n3. **Hardening in `bin/notify.sh` and the script.** `curl -sS` with output discarded exited 0 even when Telegram returned an error, so I added `-f`. The script now writes \"notify failed\" to stderr if sending fails.\n\nIf that error shows up in the log after you fix the first two, the keychain lookup in `notify.sh` may be failing under launchd. In that case, set `TG_BOT_TOKEN` in the plist environment instead.\n\nThe schedule and paths are fine. `claude` was found on the PATH, since the error is about login, not a missing command.\n\nThe explanation is in `ANSWER.md`. I made no commits and sent nothing to any external service."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"st